          "type": "any"
        }
      ],
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "data": {
        "title": "Define the recursive container and capability contract",
        "body": "Define one scale-independent model: containers own members; ports expose typed capabilities; handles render capabilities; and instantiate resolves according to the receiving container. A graph contains nodes, while a workspace contains graph instances backed by graph documents and declarations. Instantiate always means a new instance: every drop allocates a new record ID and a new semantic nodeId. Declare is the separate same-identity operation.",
        "priority": "critical",
        "status": "in-progress",
        "owner": "",
        "estimateHours": "",
        "acceptanceCriteria": [
          "The contract names graph and workspace as container scopes.",
          "The same capability shape is valid at both scopes.",
          "Identity, representation, relationship, authority, and result type are independent fields.",
          "No primitive is inferred from handle appearance or canvas coordinates alone.",
          "Instantiate allocates a new graph-local record ID and a new semantic nodeId on every drop.",
          "Repeated drops of one capability produce independent instances that retain common source provenance.",
          "Only declare may create another declaration with an existing semantic nodeId."
        ],
        "definitionKey": "task",
        "_classBinding": {
          "key": "task",
          "sourceRef": "github://twilite-zone/public/library/classes/nodes/task-planning/task.node-class.node",
          "ref": "github://twilite-zone/public/library/classes/nodes/task-planning/task.node-class.node",
