        "title": "Validate recursive instantiation end to end",
        "body": "Test the abstraction at both scales: node-handle to blank graph, graph-border handle to another graph, graph-border handle to blank workspace, and endpoint-to-endpoint relationship creation. Include undo, dirty ownership, save, reload, focus, minimaps, and semantic zoom. The first fixture browser smoke now passes graph-interior and blank-workspace drops with no page errors.",
        "priority": "high",
        "status": "todo",
        "owner": "",
        "estimateHours": "",
        "acceptanceCriteria": [
          "All three target classes resolve deterministically and produce the previewed primitive.",
          "Only the owning graph document becomes dirty after graph-level mutation.",
          "Workspace arrangement and graph instance placement remain workspace state.",
          "Duplicate drops, multiple instances of one source graph, read-only sources, Save All, close, and reopen behave coherently.",
          "Focused tests and browser smoke checks cover graph-scale and workspace-scale instantiation."
        ],
