      "data": {
        "rationale": "Instantiate allocates both a new graph-local node record ID and a new semantic nodeId. Repeating the same drop creates multiple independently owned and editable instances. They share source provenance or an instanceOf/class binding, not semantic identity. Reference creates a local carrier pointing to a different identity, while declare is the only operation that may reuse the source semantic nodeId in another graph.",
        "status": "decided",
        "decidedAt": "2026-09-09T21:10:19.109Z",
        "owner": "Michael",
